      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "FOLFIRINOX therapy has a high response rate for pancreatic carcinoma, but has serious adverse effects. FOLFIRINOX therapy was administered to 11 patients with locally advanced pancreatic carcinoma at our hospital. We investigated the usefulness of primary prophylactic administration of pegfilgrastim(PegG). In the group receiving PegG, as well as with onset of neutropenia and thrombocytopenia, febrile neutropenia was reduced. Rates of anorexia and fatigue were also lower than in those who did not receive PegG. The PegG group maintained a high average relative dose intensity, as well as a high response rate. Primary prophylactic administration of PegG in FOLFIRINOX therapy is valid for pancreatic carcinoma."},
